// Negative fixture (guard reject): a compound assignment reads its target
// before writing (`x += 1` is `x = x + 1`), so it must be rejected on an
// uninitialized variable before the program runs.
// Expected pre-run diagnostic: GuardError: UnassignedVariableCallException
// ... compound assignment reads 'x' before it is assigned on all paths.

void main() {
    int x;
    x += 1;
    printline(x);
}
